+# Delivered source excerpt
+
+Lewis Spence, *The Myths of Mexico & Peru* (1913), Chapter V, “The Maya,” “The Creation-Story,” printed p. 209; Project Gutenberg eBook 53080, <https://www.gutenberg.org/files/53080/53080-h/53080-h.htm>.
+
+> The beginning of this interesting book is taken up with the Kiche story of the creation, and what occurred directly subsequent to that event. […] He called out “Earth,” and the solid land appeared.
+
+This is Spence's English prose about a story he labels “Kiche,” not a quotation from a K'iche-language edition. The locator resolves to the printed-page marker `[209]` in the linked text.
